@host = http://localhost:5100

### 1. Report an incident (DB connection leak scenario → concurrent round, contradiction, handoff deep dive)
POST {{host}}/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "incidentId": "INC-123",
  "title": "checkout-api HTTP 500 after deployment",
  "description": "Checkout requests failing with HTTP 500 since ~14:04 UTC, shortly after a release.",
  "service": "checkout-api",
  "severity": "SEV1"
}

### 2. Follow the investigation (phase, evidence, todos, timeline)
GET {{host}}/incidents/INC-123

### 3. Pending approvals (the rollback proposed by RemediationAgent)
GET {{host}}/approvals?status=Pending

### 4. Approve (replace the id) → action executes → verification → close & learn
POST {{host}}/approvals/apr-REPLACE-ME/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approved": true, "decidedBy": "cris@oncall", "comment": "Rollback approved" }

### 5. Report (postmortem draft)
GET {{host}}/incidents/INC-123/report

### 6. Turn receipts (model, prompt/skill versions, tools, tokens, cost, latency per agent run)
GET {{host}}/incidents/INC-123/receipts

### Other scenarios
POST {{host}}/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "incidentId": "INC-124", "title": "search-api latency spike and timeouts", "service": "search-api" }

###
POST {{host}}/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "incidentId": "INC-125", "title": "payments-api failing with HTTP 502", "service": "payments-api" }

### Azure Monitor webhook (common alert schema)
POST {{host}}/webhooks/azure-monitor
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schemaId": "azureMonitorCommonAlertSchema",
  "data": {
    "essentials": {
      "alertId": "/subscriptions/xxx/providers/Microsoft.AlertsManagement/alerts/7f3c2a",
      "alertRule": "payments-api 5xx rate > 5%",
      "severity": "Sev1",
      "monitorCondition": "Fired",
      "configurationItems": [ "payments-api" ],
      "description": "HTTP 502 rate above threshold"
    }
  }
}

### Kill switch
POST {{host}}/incidents/INC-124/stop
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Handled manually by on-call" }

